 Payload paths are relative to `WORK/repo`, for example
 `--qualification ../checks/TASK/qualification/qualification.json`.
 These flags retain the existing source validation and approval boundaries.
+
+Keep command logs and later reviewer-only validation reports outside the
+inventoried `generators/TASK/workspace/parametric/evidence/` directory. From the
+outer packet, `review.py run --receipt checks/TASK/manifest-command.json ...`
+places the command receipt in `WORK/checks/TASK/`; payload output paths use
+`../checks/TASK/...` from `WORK/repo`. Do not tee manifest output into its own
+`--evidence` tree: that log changes while its inventory is being hashed. After
+manifest/preflight, place new tamper/export reports under `checks/TASK/` too.
+If bound source or inventoried evidence needs editing, rebuild its inventory
+and refresh affected receipts using the existing guarded commands; moving a
+report does not repair already-stale evidence.
+
+`review_base_preflight --out NEW_DIR` requires a path that does not exist, even
+as an empty directory. Create its parent if needed and let preflight create the
+leaf with `qualification.json` and `execution.json`; retain old runs separately.
+
+Witness templates include `(rule! (lambda (g) g))` as a standalone identity
+syntax example. It is not selected automatically and does not establish a valid
+skip-A argument; authors still supply the dependency, intermediate and ablation,
+and protected build/replay must show different final output. A bare `(rule! g)`
+has no top-level binding for `g`.
 
 For concise authoring coverage, `python3 -m arcpuzzles.review_base_preflight`
 prints job/setting counts, parametric labelled-pair counts, canonical base-pair
